Package: drumee-bootstrap
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: Role entrypoints and healthchecks for Drumee containers
 The scripts each Drumee role container runs at start, and the probes that say
 whether it is serving. One entrypoint per role — app, web, media, dns, mail,
 schemas, infra — plus a shared library holding the credential provisioning that
 was previously duplicated in every image's entrypoint.
 .
 These arrive as a versioned package rather than being copied into an image at
 build time, which is what "COPY ./opt/drumee/init.d/*" used to do: outside any
 dependency graph, unversioned, and impossible to roll back independently.
 .
 The package delivers the payload; the container executes it. Nothing here starts
 a service or touches a database during an image build.
 .
 This package name previously belonged to the interactive bare-metal installer,
 which is now drumee-installer. The version line continues upwards from that
 package so apt never reads this one as a downgrade.
